WEBVTT

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:14.440
An AI agent can use tools, such as a web browser, while it works on a task. We'll add a tool to our paper model: sending a text message. It's a way to see who does what when a model asks for help.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:26.220
Here's the rule. Fill the cup and draw, exactly as before. But the moment you draw a punctuation mark, a full stop or a comma, pause. That's a tool call.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:36.520
In our activity, the model draws punctuation like any other word. Some rows never call the tool. Some always do.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:51.420
Say you've written "here comes the dog". The row for "dog": two red for a full stop, two blue for "runs". Draw one. Red. Full stop. So pause.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:01:00.780
The tool is a text message. Send "What comes next?", and the sentence so far, to three friends or group chats.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:13.040
The first reply back, "and it wants my sandwich", is your tool result. Write the whole thing down, then the full stop you drew. Then carry on, from the full stop.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:25.540
Our sheets have no row for "sandwich". We restart from the full stop so we have a row to use. That also means the reply cannot change our model's next choice.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:38.320
Replies take time. If nothing's back, leave a gap before the punctuation mark. Write the mark and keep going from its row. Fill the gap when the first reply arrives.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:52.420
The model drew a full stop after "dog". You paused it, sent the message, and added the reply before carrying on. Those jobs make you the harness: the part that connects the model to its tools.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:02:05.560
Software can do those jobs too. In a larger model, the reply can inform what happens next: a search result might lead to another search. Our paper model always carries on from the punctuation row.

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:19.280
What would you let an agent do without asking you first? Pause here and discuss that with your group. Then try the activity, with your group doing the harness's jobs.
